WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:14.280
"Mother-in-law" is an anagram of "Hitler woman".

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.990
It is forbidden for aircraft to fly over the
Taj Mahal.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:25.789
A cat uses its whiskers to determine if a
space is too small to squeeze through.

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:31.510
There's a bookstore in Australia where books
are wrapped in paper with short descriptions

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.860
so no one can "judge a book by it's cover."

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:42.610
The U.S. spends more money per person on health
care than any other country, yet its life

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:46.309
expectancy is below average.

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:52.950
Mailing an entire building has been illegal
in the U.S. since 1916 when a man mailed a

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:59.800
40,000-ton brick house across Utah to avoid
high freight rates.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:05.360
More than 1,000 different languages are spoken
on the continent of Africa.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:13.160
Cats have over 100 vocal sounds; dogs only
have 10.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:20.869
Two-thirds of the world's caviar is eaten
aboard the Queen Elizabeth 2 cruise ship.

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:27.420
Early draft names for Walt Disney's seven
dwarfs included Flabby, Dirty, Shifty, Lazy,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.659
Burpy, Baldy and Biggo-Ego.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:35.560
A shark is the only fish that can blink with
both eyes.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:42.490
Certain frogs can be frozen solid then thawed,
and continue living.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.549
Beauty pageants for children are banned in
France.

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:53.970
They are punishable with up to 2 years in
prison and a €30,000 fine.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:02:00.799
Walt Disney was so poor in his twenties, he
had to eat dog food.

00:02:00.799 --> 00:02:05.510
The smallest trees in the world are the dwarf
willows of Greenland.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:08.079
They are two inches tall

00:02:08.079 --> 00:02:19.319
Albanian has 27 words for different kinds
of moustache and 30 for eyebrows.

